==Solution 5 (Much easier if you notice the one line construction + use properties of the golden ratio)==

We will start with a similar diagram to all of the other submitted solutions with ONE difference: We will connect line segment <imath>CR</imath> to form a <imath>36^\circ</imath>-<imath>36^\circ</imath>-<imath>108^\circ</imath> golden triangle <imath>\triangle CPR</imath>. We know this is a <imath>36^\circ</imath>-<imath>36^\circ</imath>-<imath>108^\circ</imath> golden triangle because <imath>QR</imath> is the perpendicular bisector of <imath>CP</imath> (in order to fold vertex <imath>C</imath> onto the center <imath>P</imath>), so <imath>\triangle CPR</imath> must be isosceles, with angle <imath>\angle CPR = \frac{360^\circ}{10} = 36^\circ</imath> due to the regular pentagon.

